{"version":"1","id":"artsy","handle":"artsy","name":"Artsy.net","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/d72060ae77ca4103b2c34329b400a673","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":1.8346,"y":-0.2563,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":12,"newest_post_at":"2026-01-09T00:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-09-10T00:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.083333,"avg_read_time":6.166667,"summary_length_avg":318.25,"title_length_avg":40.333333,"title_length_var":108.222222,"tag_entropy":3.198872,"tag_diversity":2.166667,"top_tag_share":0.0,"avg_upvotes":0.666667,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.166667,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.333333,"zero_engagement_share":0.833333,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.11316,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.090909},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-4.75,9.4559],"cadence_depth":[-9.5441,0.6324],"hype_variety":[-9.3824,0.0588],"title_style":[8.1765,-9.1471]},"top_tags":[["react-native",2],["react",2],["webdev",2],["typescript",2],["cicd",2],["rails",2],["cypress",2],["testing",2]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Two years of Next.js at Artsy: A Retrospective","The Checklist for Deploying a Scary Change","How Artsy improved their React Native apps in 2025"],"outlier":["Artsy Engineering"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"mZ1GeIDQJ","title":"How Artsy improved their React Native apps in 2025","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2026/01/09/artsy-mobile-2025-wrapped/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/artsy-mobile-2025-wrapped-mz1geidqj","summary":"Artsy's mobile team shares their 2025 improvements across three React Native apps. Major achievements include migrating to Expo, adopting React Native's new architecture, and refactoring navigation to use react-navigation exclusively. Performance optimizations reduced TTI to under 100ms through query splitting, speculative prefetching, and CDN caching. Infrastructure improvements include migrating to GitHub Actions (reducing Android build time by 75%), implementing E2E tests with Maestro, and improving keyboard handling with react-native-keyboard-controller. Developer experience enhancements include Rozenite debugging plugins, mise for environment management, and better beta build workflows.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/fce9bd7d58bbe1da2c57c25a8db609e7?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"l4mYcVfSs","title":"Two years of Next.js at Artsy: A Retrospective","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2024/03/07/nextjs-at-artsy-retrospective/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/two-years-of-next-js-at-artsy-a-retrospective-l4mycvfss","summary":"Artsy shares their experience with Next.js over the past two years, including the success of rebuilding their internal tools app, the excitement around Next 13 and React Server Components, and the challenges and limitations they encountered during the migration process.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c9daa248414eba853d760bf9bda9eb2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2024-03-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"BDPKSFWSN","title":"The Checklist for Deploying a Scary Change","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2023/09/13/deploying-a-scary-change/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-checklist-for-deploying-a-scary-change-bdpksfwsn","summary":"A checklist for deploying risky changes, including plans for rolling back and monitoring for issues. The checklist helps in increasing confidence and reducing incidents.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c9daa248414eba853d760bf9bda9eb2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-13T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"egUrZ6YRA","title":"Artsy Engineering","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2023/03/01/typescript-magic/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/artsy-engineering-egurz6yra","summary":"Artsy Engineering discusses a TypeScript trick to achieve autocomplete and type checking for specific string types while allowing for general string support.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c9daa248414eba853d760bf9bda9eb2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-03-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"M50xir0ED","title":"Are you using the right Mongo geospatial query?","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2023/02/10/mongo-geospatial-queries/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/are-you-using-the-right-mongo-geospatial-query--m50xir0ed","summary":"The post discusses an issue where a partner gallery was not showing up on Los Angeles exhibition listings despite being within the specified radius. It explores the geospatial query in MongoDB and the use of $center and $centerSphere. It also touches on map distortion and its impact on geospatial queries.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c9daa248414eba853d760bf9bda9eb2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-02-10T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"fqJH10fRo","title":"Parallelizing Jest and Cypress.io Tests on CircleCI","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2022/09/07/quick-tips-to-speed-up-ci/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/parallelizing-jest-and-cypress-io-tests-on-circleci-fqjh10fro","summary":"Learn how to parallelize tests in Jest using the sharding feature and how to parallelize Cypress.io integration tests on CircleCI using the split command.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c9daa248414eba853d760bf9bda9eb2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-09-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"u7OifTnWf","title":"Hacking Around Safari's 7-day Cookie Limit","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2022/08/23/getting-around-7-day-cookie/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/hacking-around-safari-s-7-day-cookie-limit-u7oiftnwf","summary":"Discover how to bypass Safari's 7-day cookie limit by overwriting client-side cookies with server-side cookies.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c9daa248414eba853d760bf9bda9eb2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-08-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"mYr0pMYha","title":"Third Time's the Charm: Deprecating KAWS","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2022/05/09/deprecating-kaws/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/third-time-s-the-charm-deprecating-kaws-myr0pmyha","summary":"Artsy deprecates KAWS, a server app with its own Mongo database and GraphQL API, and folds its functionality into Artsy's main database and API, Gravity. This decision was made due to its idiosyncratic stack, extra hops on each request, lack of admin UI, and the lack of relationships between collections and artworks. Artsy planned the deprecation by scoping it tightly, and the tech plan was the result of multiple attempts. Lessons learned include the importance of keeping the scope focused, avoiding naming projects after artists, and the challenges of feature flagging a GraphQL service.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c9daa248414eba853d760bf9bda9eb2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-05-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"FIi7eIDko","title":"Stepping Out Of The Knowledge Zone","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2022/04/13/stepping-out-of-the-knowledge-zone/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/stepping-out-of-the-knowledge-zone-fii7eidko","summary":"The author, a backend engineer, shares their experience of stepping out of their comfort zone and joining the velocity team. They initially had reservations due to being a woman in a male-dominated team, but found support and mentorship. They learned new technologies, such as Docker and JavaScript, and successfully contributed to projects like integrity and the new-admin. Their positive experience led to a desire to join the velocity team permanently.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c9daa248414eba853d760bf9bda9eb2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-04-13T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"a1fcNnlCg","title":"Using Context to Simplify a VERY Large React Form","url":"https://artsy.github.io/blog/2022/02/01/using-context-to-simplify-a-react-form/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/using-context-to-simplify-a-very-large-react-form-a1fcnnlcg","summary":"Artsy's Artwork Form, a large React form, underwent a conversion process to simplify its structure and improve developer experience. The form had issues with prop drilling, type checking, and tight coupling of components. The conversion involved creating a hook to use the Formik context, converting components to functional and TypeScript, and reducing prop drilling. The form is now easier to understand and the next steps include breaking it up into smaller forms.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/7c9daa248414eba853d760bf9bda9eb2?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-01T00:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["showmax","doordash","ntietz","37signals","developerdao"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","on_leuwcq","horde","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"showmax","handle":"showmax","name":"Showmax Engineering","is_squad":false,"x":1.7682,"y":-0.0484,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":66,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/eb82b83d0fa346a1910495fee2412e5e","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.465793,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.007576,"avg_read_time":5.136364,"tag_diversity":0.893939},"top_tags_preview":[["testing",8],["general-programming",6],["ruby",5]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-6.0294,0.1029],"cadence_depth":[-2.5588,-2.0588],"hype_variety":[0.1618,6.3